ovement explains ≤2.4pp (7.6%) of 31.3% C rate; item-level characteristics dominate (pseudo R²=0.0423)\n- **plan_020_result.json**: Circularity ablation—DIF removal is least disruptive among non-random strategies (ρ=0.9970 vs 0.9657 for accuracy gap); DIF captures specific signal, not general item quality\n- **plan_021_result.json**: Non-uniform DIF analysis—38.7% of items show non-uniform DIF; temporal shift involves both difficulty and discrimination changes\n- **plan_022_result.json**: Model independence—graduated de-duplication shows C% driven by sample size, not model redundancy; 31.3% C-rate robust to family structure\n- **plan_023_result.json**: Item characterization—DIF-C items harder (d=-0.247), higher discrimination (d=0.230); strong difficulty×direction correlation (ρ=-0.597)\n- **plan_026_result.json**: ConStat comparison—DIF-C vs web contamination nearly orthogonal (enrichment=0.964, Jaccard=0.206); completely different signals\n\n### **3. REGISTRY FILES**\n\n- **/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/dream_registry.yaml** — Dream/review cycle history (7 dreams, multiple revisions, EMNLP 2026 venue)\n- **/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/registry.yaml** — Comprehensive experiment registry with all 27 plans, MVPs, power simulations, and status tracking\n- **/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/global/logs/workers/registry.json** — Global worker task registry documenting all executed tasks\n\n### **4. METRICS & DATA FILES (CSV/Excel)**\n\nComprehensive metrics across experiments (~114,115 lines of CSV data total):\n\n**Core results CSVs:**\n- `/artifacts/_project/data/gsm8k_dif_results.csv` — GSM8K temporal DIF analysis (290KB, ~4000+ items)\n- `/artifacts/_project/data/lr_dif_item_results.csv` — Logistic Regression DIF with uniform/non-uniform classification (306KB, 1787 items × 9 columns)\n- `/artifacts/plan_020/circularity_ablation_results.csv` — Item re